F = 0.036 / 0.09 = 0.4 N (repulsive)', 10),
(8, 'Electrostatics', 'easy', 'A 10 µF and a 20 µF capacitor are connected in series. What is the equivalent capacitance?', '["30 µF","15 µF","6.67 µF","5 µF"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Series capacitors: Ceq = (C1 × C2)/(C1 + C2)
Ceq = (10 × 20)/(10 + 20) = 200/30 = 6.67 µF', 10),
(9, 'Electrostatics', 'medium', 'How much energy is stored in a 100 µF capacitor charged to 200 V?', '["0.02 J","1 J","2 J","4 J"]'::jsonb, 2, 'W = ½ C V²
W = ½ (100×10⁻⁶)(200)² = ½ (100×10⁻⁶)(40,000) = 2 J', 15),
(10, 'Electromagnetic Induction', 'medium', 'A coil of 200 turns is linked by a flux that changes uniformly from 0.05 Wb to 0.01 Wb in 0.2 s. What is the average induced emf?', '["8 V","10 V","40 V","200 V"]'::jsonb, 2, 'e = N (ΔΦ/Δt)
